{title: I Lift My Eyes to the Hills}
{subtitle: Psalm 121}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 108}
{time: 2/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Bb] | [Eb] |
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Bb] | [F] |
| [Bb] | [Bb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
I lift my eyes up to the [Eb]hills
Where does my help [F]come from
[Bb]My help comes from the Lord a[Eb]bove
[Bb]Who made [F]the heaven and [Bb]earth
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
He will not let your foot [Eb]slip
[Bb]He who keeps you will not [F]sleep
[Bb]The Lord will watch your going [Eb]out
[Bb]And your [F]coming [Bb]in
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Bb] | [Bb] |
| [Eb] | [Bb] | [Bb] | [Bb] |
| [F] | [Bb] | [Bb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
The Lord is your keeper and your [Eb]shade
Up[Bb]on your right [F]hand
The [Bb]sun won't strike you in the [Eb]day
[Bb]Nor the [F]moon by [Bb]night
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
He will not let your foot [Eb]slip
[Bb]He who keeps you will not [F]sleep
The [Bb]Lord will watch your going [Eb]out
[Bb]And your [F]coming [Bb]in
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Outro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Bb] | [Bb] |
